<article class="env-lemma" id="04PY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04PY">Lemma <span data-tag="04PY">33.7.15</span>.</a> Let $K/k$ be an extension of fields. Let $X$ be a scheme over $k$. For every connected component $T$ of $X$ the inverse image $T_ K \subset X_ K$ is a union of connected components of $X_ K$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a purely topological statement. Denote $p : X_ K \to X$ the projection morphism. Let $T \subset X$ be a connected component of $X$. Let $t \in T_ K = p^{-1}(T)$. Let $C \subset X_ K$ be a connected component containing $t$. Then $p(C)$ is a connected subset of $X$ which meets $T$, hence $p(C) \subset T$. Hence $C \subset T_ K$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>